"I'm sick and tired of being sick and tired."--Fanny Lou Hamer

		WHY WE MUST GO TO CHICAGO IN '96!!...


We must go to Chicago.  "Generation X" must go...People of Color
must go...Gay Americans must go...Native Americans must go...
We ALL must go!!  We can wait no longer.  How many more people 
must die from pollution?  How many more children must go hungry 
and homeless?  How much longer must we stand by and watch "the 
powers that be" persist with stalemate, in-house bickering, 
"politics-as-usual"...auctioning off our nation's future to the 
highest bidder.

In 1996 the Democratic Party will return to Chicago...and we will 
be there to greet them.  People are going to stream in from all 
over the land to be a part of a new beginning.  The dawn of what 
this nation can be, should be, is just below the horizon...and it 
is up to us to bring it forth.  In 1968, the world watched as 
thousands of energetic and angry Americans travelled to Chicago 
to the Democratic National Convention.  They rose up and demanded 
a better future for America.  They called on their government 
and the men who controlled it to once again be accountable to the 
people.  They challenged the status quo.  They challenged the 
political process in this country to truly work for them...for 
you and for me...for all Americans.  And the world looked on 
as the status quo struck back with violence and repression... 
as blood was spilled and ideas were silenced.  

This time...history will not repeat itself.  This time there 
are too many of us...too many people of all races, classes, 
ages and upbringings...people who will no longer tolerate the 
mortgaging of America's future.  We will no longer tolerate 
the polluting of our air and water.  We will no longer 
tolerate a facade of democracy...We demand the real thing.

We will be there in Chicago in 1996.  We will reform the 
Democratic Party into what it should be...the people's party.
We already have a Republican Party in America...we don't need two.
The rhetoric of the Democratic Party must become a reality...

Many will claim that we will kill the Democratic Party.  
Many will ask us to reconsider...reminding us that we must 
go along to get along.  But that philosophy has gotten us 
nowhere.  If the Democratic Party won't be the people's 
party then it's time for the funeral.  The mourners will 
have a place with the GOP.  When Americans have a TRUE choice 
between a progressive agenda for ALL people, and the same old 
tired rhetoric of the current political class, they will 
choose the path that leads forward, rather then around in circles.

We are going to need you.  We are going to need farm workers, and
factory workers.  We are going to need PhD's and retirees.  We 
are going to need the young, the old, the North, the South, the 
East, the West...and all the rest.  WE ARE GOING TO NEED YOU.

We all share certain things.  We all need housing, healthcare, 
and education.  We all need clean water and clean air.  We all 
need safe streets and freedom from want and fear.  Let us
look towards what binds us all together rather than what 
separates us.  United we can put the power where it belongs
...in the hands of the people.  Together we can set the nation on 
a path that leads to a truly better place...for everyone.

We are going to need you.  We are all in this together...
and it's only together that we can rise to our greatest 
potential.  A potential that will lead to change and a better
quality of life.  We will not go to Chicago to be violent.  
We will go to Chicago to take back what is ours, and to give 
to the people who can't join us a glimpse of what could be.

But...we are going to need you.

